{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Graph-shaped collections for Swift: search trees, tries, suffix structures, decision diagrams,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range and spatial trees, ropes, persistent trees and caches, with value semantics, built on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Grafluent.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/ChoosingASearchTree","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import GrafluentCollections"},{"type":"text","text":" imports every module. Each module also has its own documentation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and can be imported on its own."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import GrafluentCollections","","var scores: FenwickTree = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6]","print(scores.prefixSum(through: 3))  \/\/ 9","print(scores.sum(in: 2 ..< 6))       \/\/ 19"]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Values, not references","anchor":"Values-not-references"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every collection is a copy-on-write struct. Assigning one copies nothing until one of the copies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is mutated; then only that copy pays, once, and the other keeps its elements:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let original: BTree = [1, 2, 3]","var copy = original","copy.insert(4)","Array(original)   \/\/ [1, 2, 3]","Array(copy)       \/\/ [1, 2, 3, 4]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices of a tree live in flat arrays linked by integer indices rather than in a class per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex, so a copy is a few array copies and a traversal reads memory almost in order. The API"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"follows the standard library and Swift Collections: the sorted sets are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SetAlgebra"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"random-access collections indexed by rank, the dictionaries take "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subscript(_:default:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range trees are collections of their values."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Traps and checked spellings","anchor":"Traps-and-checked-spellings"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A plain spelling traps when its precondition fails, like an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"type":"text","text":" subscript out of range: it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the fast path, for callers who know the precondition holds. Beside it, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checked:"},{"type":"text","text":" spelling"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws a typed error instead, one of those in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/collectionerrors","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try?"},{"type":"text","text":" turns it into an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let primes: AVLTree = [2, 3, 5, 7]","primes[2]                    \/\/ 5","try primes[checked: 9]       \/\/ throws IndexOutOfRange"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A mutation that would break a structure’s invariant, such as joining two treaps whose elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interleave, throws on its plain spelling and changes nothing. Where the standard library’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collections return an optional ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a dictionary’s subscript, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"min()"},{"type":"text","text":"), these do too."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Grafluent conversions","anchor":"Grafluent-conversions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A collection whose shape is a tree converts to the Grafluent type of that shape: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootedTree"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree"},{"text":", with an initializer on the Grafluent type that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"costs O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") once. Structures whose shape is a general graph, such as decision diagrams and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automata, offer a view that is a Grafluent graph without copying. Either way, Grafluent’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms, drawings and file formats run over the collection; its own operations never go","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through the conversion. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"},{"text":" shows the round trip.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Modules","anchor":"Modules"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Group"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Modules"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Search trees","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees","type":"reference"},{"text":" (AVL, red–black and splay trees, treaps), ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees","type":"reference"},{"text":" (B-trees), ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","type":"reference"},{"text":" (skip lists)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tries","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/tries","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (tries over any sequence of symbols, radix and Patricia trees, Aho–Corasick automata)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Suffix structures"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/suffixstructures"},{"type":"text","text":" (suffix arrays with LCP, suffix trees, suffix automata)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Decision diagrams","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (reduced ordered BDDs, zero-suppressed ZDDs)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Range and spatial trees","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/rangetrees","type":"reference"},{"text":" (Fenwick trees, segment trees with lazy propagation, interval trees), ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/spatialtrees","type":"reference"},{"text":" (k-d trees, quadtrees, octrees)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sequences and persistence","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/ropes"},{"type":"text","text":" (ropes: sequences as balanced trees of chunks), "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees"},{"type":"text","text":" (path-copying weight-balanced trees that keep every version)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Caches"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/caches","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (LRU caches)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shared"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"overridingTitle":"CollectionErrors","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/collectionerrors","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"code":"CollectionErrors","type":"codeVoice"}],"isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": the errors the ","type":"text"},{"code":"checked:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" spellings throw, re-exported by every module that throws them","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/grafluentcollections"]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"GrafluentCollections","modules":[{"name":"GrafluentCollections"}],"role":"collection","title":"GrafluentCollections"},"references":{"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/tries":{"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/tries","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tries"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/tries","type":"link","title":"Tries"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/rangetrees":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/rangetrees","title":"RangeTrees","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RangeTrees"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/rangetrees"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/RangeAndSpatialTrees":{"abstract":[{"text":"Answer queries over ranges of a sequence, over intervals, and over points in space.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/rangeandspatialtrees","title":"Range and spatial trees","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","type":"topic","role":"article"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/collectionerrors":{"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/collectionerrors","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/collec